From 77c8c8fbae4279a8e988517a7e539e1c423204b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PeGa <pablo@pega.sh>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 03:20:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rewrite: clean driver pattern, 1061 lines total

- services/database.sh: single point of contact with sqlite3.
  SQLAlchemy-like API: db_start_session, db_end_session, db_pause_session,
  db_resume_session, db_flip_flag, db_insert_session, db_list_sessions,
  db_get_total_time, db_set_description, etc. Nothing else touches sqlite3.

- services/cron.sh: cron_install / cron_remove, one responsibility.
- services/focus-function.sh: PROMPT_COMMAND hook + focus() wrapper.
- config.sh: 12 lines of env var defaults. No functions. No self-sourcing.
- focus.sh: 22-line dispatcher. Fixed shift-before-use bug. Exports REFOCUS_ROOT.

lib/ commands are thin orchestration: get input -> validate lightly -> call driver -> format output.
No SQL in lib files. No validation frameworks. No parallel formatting systems.

Removes: helpers/, storage/, logger.sh, error_handling.sh, date-utils.sh,
         export.sh, import.sh, the stale root-level 'work' and 'focus' wrappers.

export/import deferred to next iteration.
